            <ArticleTitle>Decoration of exfoliated black phosphorus with nickel nanoparticles and its application in catalysis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>10946-10949</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c7cc05906j</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Nickel nanoparticles were dispersed on the surface of exfoliated black phosphorus and the resulting nanohybrid Ni/2DBP showed an improved stability with respect to pristine 2D BP when kept under ambient conditions in the dark. Ni/2DBP was applied as a catalyst in the semihydrogenation of phenylacetylene and exhibited high conversion and selectivity towards styrene. These features were preserved after recycling tests revealing the high stability of the nanohybrid.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
